{"book":10,"chapter":28,"rubric":"LEARNING RUST / THE STANDARD LIBRARY / CHAPTER 28","slides":[{"title":"Time, numbers, memory","sub":"Chapter 28 · What's in std","short":"Intro","main":"Time and numbers in std; calendars and randomness are crates.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Time","Numbers","Memory"],"captions":["Duration and Instant: a span and a moment as separate types","Hundreds of integer and float methods; special types Wrapping, Saturating, NonZero","size_of, align_of and the mem module; calendars, big numbers, randomness are external crates"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Duration","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Instant","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":50.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"i32","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":136.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"f64","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":222.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Wrapping","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a3","x":308.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"NonZero","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":50.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"size_of","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":136.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"mem","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":222.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"chrono","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a3","x":308.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"rand","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[5.5,21.8]}]},{"title":"Duration","sub":"Duration","short":"Duration","main":"Create, read, arithmetic, safe operations.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Create","Read and arithmetic","Safety"],"captions":["Duration::from_secs, from_millis, from_micros, from_nanos, from_secs_f64","as_secs, as_millis, as_secs_f64, subsec_nanos; + − × number and comparison","checked_add, checked_sub, saturating_sub; no negative durations; {:?} prints \"1.5s\""],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["Duration::from_secs(90)","Duration::from_millis(1500)","Duration::from_secs_f64(0.25)"],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["d.as_secs_f64()   // 1.5","d * 2 + Duration::from_secs(1)","a > b"],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["a.checked_sub(b)         // Option","a.saturating_sub(b)      // 0 if b > a"],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[14.4,31.5]}]},{"title":"Instant and SystemTime","sub":"Two kinds of moments","short":"Instant","main":"Measuring: Instant; stamps: SystemTime; calendar: crates.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Instant","SystemTime","Calendar"],"captions":["Instant is a monotonic clock: forward only, for measuring; elapsed() returns a Duration","SystemTime is a wall clock, can jump; duration_since(UNIX_EPOCH) gives seconds since 1970","Calendar, time zones, date formatting: chrono or time; not in std"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let t = Instant::now();","work();","println!(\"{:?}\", t.elapsed());"],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["SystemTime::now()","    .duration_since(UNIX_EPOCH)?"],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"measuring\nInstant","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"dates\nchrono / time","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[17.1,30.9]}]},{"title":"Pauses and measuring","sub":"sleep and black_box","short":"Pauses","main":"sleep, timeouts, black_box, criterion.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["sleep","Timeout","black_box"],"captions":["thread::sleep(d) puts a thread to sleep; in async use an async sleep, or the whole executor stalls","Timeout: remember Instant::now() and check elapsed() < limit","The compiler drops unused computations: std::hint::black_box; for serious measuring, criterion"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["thread::sleep(Duration::from_millis(100));"],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let start = Instant::now();","while start.elapsed() < limit { }"],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["let r = black_box(compute());","// criterion: many runs, statistics"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[12.6,29.8]}]},{"title":"Integers","sub":"Methods","short":"Integers","main":"checked, wrapping, bits, powers of two.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["checked, wrapping…","Bits","Powers of two"],"captions":["checked_*, wrapping_*, saturating_*, overflowing_*; abs_diff, rem_euclid, pow, checked_pow","count_ones, leading_zeros, trailing_zeros, rotate_left, swap_bytes, reverse_bits, to_be_bytes","is_power_of_two, next_power_of_two; isqrt, ilog2: integer root and logarithm"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["a.checked_add(b)","a.wrapping_mul(b)","a.abs_diff(b)","a.rem_euclid(m)"],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["x.count_ones()","x.leading_zeros()","x.rotate_left(3)","x.to_be_bytes()"],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["x.is_power_of_two()","x.next_power_of_two()","n.isqrt()   n.ilog2()"],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[12.5,29.9]}]},{"title":"Floats","sub":"Methods","short":"Floats","main":"Rounding, functions, checks, total_cmp.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Rounding","Functions","Checks"],"captions":["floor, ceil, round, trunc, fract; powi, powf, sqrt, cbrt, hypot, mul_add","exp, ln, log10, log2; sin, cos, tan, asin, acos, atan2; constants in std::f64::consts","is_nan, is_finite, is_infinite; EPSILON, MIN, MAX, INFINITY; to_bits; total_cmp: a total order"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["x.floor()  x.ceil()  x.round()","x.trunc()  x.fract()","x.powi(3)   x.sqrt()   a.hypot(b)"],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["x.exp()   x.ln()   x.log10()","x.sin()   x.cos()   y.atan2(x)","std::f64::consts::PI"],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["x.is_nan()   x.is_finite()","f64::EPSILON   f64::MAX","a.total_cmp(&b)"],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[12.7,25.8]}]},{"title":"Not in std","sub":"num-*, rand","short":"Not in std","main":"No Number trait, no big numbers, no random.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["No Number","num-*","rand"],"captions":["No common \"number\" trait: generic code is written with traits like Add, Mul","num-traits (Zero, One, Num), num-bigint, num-rational, num-complex are separate crates","Randomness is the rand crate: it needs an OS entropy source; not in std"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"trait Number ✕","tone":"red","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Add + Mul + Copy","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":50.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"num-traits","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":136.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"bigint","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":222.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"rational","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a3","x":308.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"complex","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":60.0,"w":230.0,"h":34.0,"text":"rand: outside std","tone":"yellow","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[13.6,27.7]}]},{"title":"Special types","sub":"Wrapping, NonZero","short":"Special","main":"Wrapping, Saturating, NonZero and niches.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Wrapping, Saturating","NonZero","Niche"],"captions":["Wrapping(255u8) + Wrapping(1) = Wrapping(0) always, even in debug; Saturating stops at the bound","NonZeroU32 is never zero: zero is freed up for \"none\"; Option<NonZeroU32> is the size of u32","A niche works with references, Box, some enums; errors: ParseIntError, TryFromIntError"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["Wrapping(255u8) + Wrapping(1)   // 0","Saturating(250u8) + Saturating(10)   // 255"],"lang":"rust","size":9.0,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"u32 · 4 bytes","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Option<NonZero>\n4 bytes","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Option<&T>\n= size of &T","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Option<Box<T>>\n= size of Box","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[13.2,30.9]}]},{"title":"Sizes","sub":"size_of and layout","short":"Sizes","main":"Sizes of &T, &str, String, dyn; cache.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Type sizes","Layout","Cache"],"captions":["&T is 1 word; &[T], &str are 2; String, Vec are 3; Box<dyn Trait> is 2 (pointer and method table)","enum is the largest variant plus a tag (the tag hides in a niche); struct fields get reordered; repr(C) forbids it","Structs that fit in a cache line (64 bytes) are processed several times faster"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":50.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"&T 8","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":136.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"&str 16","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":222.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"String 24","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a3","x":308.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"dyn 16","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["size_of::<Option<u8>>()    // 2","size_of::<Option<&u8>>()   // 8"],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":60.0,"w":240.0,"h":34.0,"text":"64 bytes = cache line","tone":"yellow","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[17.3,26.7]}]},{"title":"Low-level","sub":"transmute and others","short":"mem","main":"transmute, ManuallyDrop, MaybeUninit, discriminant.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["transmute","ManuallyDrop, MaybeUninit","discriminant"],"captions":["transmute reinterprets bytes and needs unsafe; there is almost always a safe alternative (from_bits, to_ne_bytes)","ManuallyDrop turns off the automatic destructor; MaybeUninit is a value without initialization","mem::discriminant(&e) is the variant number without parsing data; unsafe doesn't turn off type checks"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["unsafe { std::mem::transmute::<u32, f32>(x) }","f32::from_bits(x)   // safe"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":9.0,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"ManuallyDrop","tone":"red","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"MaybeUninit","tone":"red","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["mem::discriminant(&a) == mem::discriminant(&b)"],"lang":"rust","size":9.0,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[13.6,25.7]}]},{"title":"Hash and randomness","sub":"Hasher and PRNG","short":"Hash","main":"SipHash, stable hashes, your own generator.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Hasher","Stable hash","Own generator"],"captions":["std::hash: Hash and Hasher; SipHash resists attacks","A SipHash result changes from run to run, so don't store it; for stable hashes use blake3, sha2, fxhash","A linear congruential generator is 5 lines and wrapping_mul; in tests take the generator as a parameter"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["let mut h = DefaultHasher::new();","x.hash(&mut h);   let v = h.finish();"],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"SipHash\nrandom salt","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"blake3, sha2\nstable","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["state = state.wrapping_mul(6364136223846793005)","    .wrapping_add(1442695040888963407);"],"lang":"rust","size":8.0,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[13.2,25.1]}]},{"title":"Memory allocation","sub":"Heap and arenas","short":"Allocators","main":"global_allocator, arenas.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Heap","Own allocator","Arenas"],"captions":["Box, Vec, String live on the heap; the global allocator hands it out","#[global_allocator] replaces it: jemalloc, mimalloc speed up many programs","Many small objects: an arena, one big allocation and offsets (bumpalo, typed-arena)"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"stack\nfast, small","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"heap\nflexible","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["#[global_allocator]","static A: mimalloc::MiMalloc = mimalloc::MiMalloc;"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"a thousand Boxes\na thousand allocations","tone":"red","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"arena\none allocation","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[8.8,28.0]}]},{"title":"Summary","sub":"What's next","short":"Summary","main":"Next: the catalog of std traits.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Remember","Cheat sheet","Next"],"captions":["Instant for measuring, SystemTime for stamps; Duration has no negative values","Integers and floats: hundreds of methods; Wrapping, Saturating, NonZero; size_of; num and rand are external","Next chapter: the catalog of traits: Clone, Copy, Default, Eq, Ord, Hash, From, AsRef and more"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":50.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Duration","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":136.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Instant","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":222.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"num","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a3","x":308.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"mem","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let t = Instant::now();","let s = n.checked_mul(m)?;"],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":60.0,"w":250.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Clone · Copy · Default · Eq · Ord · Hash","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[15.1,24.3]}]}]}